---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Cookies, Analytics & Ads | StudyRoadmap" description="StudyRoadmap privacy policy: Google Analytics 4, local storage, Monetag ad cookies and push notifications, Consent Mode, and how to opt out of personalised ads.">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://studyroadmap.in/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Privacy Policy","item":"https://studyroadmap.in/privacy/"}]})}>
  </script>
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content" class="flex-1">
    <section class="bg-surface-50 dark:bg-surface-950 border-b border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
      <div class="container-page py-14 text-center">
        <h1 class="heading-1 text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-50">Privacy Policy</h1>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="container-page py-14 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-6 text-sm text-surface-300 leading-relaxed">
        <p><strong class="text-surface-50">Effective date:</strong> 15 September 2026 (advertising partner updated: Monetag replaced Google AdSense; self-hosted analytics added)</p>
        <p>StudyRoadmap™ is built with privacy as a core principle. We collect <strong class="text-surface-50">as little data as possible</strong> while still understanding how the site is used.</p>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-50 mb-2">What We Collect</h2>
          <p>We use <strong class="text-surface-50">Google Analytics 4</strong> (measurement ID <code class="text-xs">G-XPWXLW8J3R</code>) to measure aggregated traffic and page performance. GA4 may process technical data such as approximate location (city/country derived from IP), device/browser type, pages viewed, referrers, and session duration. We do not use GA4 to identify you by name, and we do not upload student lists or exam choices to Google Analytics. IP anonymization is enabled in our GA configuration.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Our self-hosted nginx server also logs standard request metadata (IP, user-agent, referrer) in access logs for security and operations. We do not sell personal data. Exam selection and study-plan preferences stay in your browser's local storage and are not sent to our servers as account data.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-50 mb-2">Consent Mode (EEA, UK, Switzerland)</h2>
          <p>Visitors in the <strong class="text-surface-50">EEA, United Kingdom and Switzerland</strong> see a cookie banner and are asked before anything non-essential loads. It offers three choices: <em>Accept all</em>, <em>Reject all</em>, or <em>Manage preferences</em> to allow advertising and analytics independently. Until you make a choice, no advertising loader and no analytics tag runs. If you reject, the site still works normally — you simply see no ads and are not measured.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Your decision is stored in your browser's local storage under the key <code class="text-xs">sr:consent</code> and is applied consistently to Google Analytics, our self-hosted analytics and the Monetag ad loaders. You can change or withdraw it at any time with the button below.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            <button type="button" onclick="window.srOpenConsent && window.srOpenConsent()" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-brand-600 px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-semibold text-white hover:bg-brand-700 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-brand-400">Manage cookie preferences</button>
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">We also implement <strong class="text-surface-50">Google Consent Mode v2</strong> defaults before the analytics tag loads. Advertising storage signals (<code class="text-xs">ad_storage</code>, <code class="text-xs">ad_user_data</code>, <code class="text-xs">ad_personalization</code>) default to denied for all regions and are only updated if you grant advertising consent. Outside the restricted regions above, analytics storage defaults to granted for aggregated site measurement only.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-50 mb-2">Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
          <p>We use your browser's <strong class="text-surface-50">local storage</strong> to save exam selection and duration preferences. That data stays on your device. Google Analytics and our advertising partner <strong class="text-surface-50">Monetag</strong> may set first- or third-party cookies or use similar storage for analytics and ad measurement. You can clear cookies and local storage anytime in browser settings. For advertising opt-outs, see the Advertising section below. You can also use browser controls or Google's tools described in the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-50 mb-2">Your Data Rights</h2>
          <p>Depending on where you live (including the EEA, UK, Switzerland, and India), you may have rights to access, correct, erase, restrict, port, or object to processing of personal data. Analytics data held by Google is governed by Google's terms and privacy policy; we will help route legitimate requests. For concerns about our server access logs or this policy, contact us at the addresses below.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-50 mb-2">Third-Party Services</h2>
          <p>We operate <strong class="text-surface-50">self-hosted analytics (Umami)</strong> on our own server at studyroadmap.in to measure which pages are used. It is cookieless, does not fingerprint devices, does not track you across other websites, honours the browser's Do Not Track signal, and the data never leaves infrastructure we control. It loads only when analytics is allowed under the consent rules above. Alongside it we use <strong class="text-surface-50">Google Analytics 4</strong> (googletagmanager.com / google-analytics.com), <strong class="text-surface-50">Google Fonts</strong> (fonts.googleapis.com, fonts.gstatic.com) for typography, and we self-host the site on <strong class="text-surface-50">nginx</strong>. Google Analytics is <strong class="text-surface-50">measurement-only</strong> on this site: we do not use Google advertising products, so no DoubleClick or DART advertising cookies are set here, and AdSense was removed on 15 September 2026. Google receives technical request data governed by the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">Google Privacy Policy</a>. Advertisements are served by <strong class="text-surface-50">Monetag</strong> (monetag.com), an advertising network operated by PropellerAds, which sets its own cookies or browser storage under the <a href="https://monetag.com/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">Monetag Privacy Policy</a>. You retain the right to access, correct, erase, restrict, port, or object to processing of any personal data held by these providers — contact us at the email below and we will route the request.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-50 mb-2">Advertising (Monetag)</h2>
          <p>We display advertisements through <strong class="text-surface-50">Monetag</strong> (monetag.com), an advertising network operated by PropellerAds. Monetag serves formats such as in-page push, browser push notifications, vignette/interstitial, and onclick/popunder. These formats may use cookies, browser storage, or — for browser push notifications — the notification permission you grant in your browser, in order to measure and personalise advertising.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Browser push notifications are opt-in at the browser level. You can decline or revoke that permission at any time in your browser settings, and none of our ad formats require you to grant it. Visit our site with <code class="text-xs">?noads=1</code> or clear site data to suppress ad loaders for your visit.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">Monetag's handling of data is governed by the <a href="https://monetag.com/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">Monetag Privacy Policy</a>. You can opt out of interest-based advertising from participating companies at <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">aboutads.info/choices</a> or the EU industry page at <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 hover:underline">youronlinechoices.eu</a>. Clearing cookies and site data in your browser removes any advertising identifiers we or our partners have set.</p>
          <p class="mt-2">For visitors in the EEA, United Kingdom and Switzerland, <strong class="text-surface-50">no ad format loads until you grant advertising consent</strong>. If you reject, you see no ads at all. If you accept, you receive the same formats as other regions, including the onclick/popunder format, which is frequency-capped to once every 12 hours and suppressed on the first interaction with the page. We do not sell personal information collected for advertising, and ad placement never influences our exam recommendations, topic priorities, or study guidance.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-50 mb-2">Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>Our site is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect any information from anyone under 13. If you believe a child under 13 has provided personal information through our site, please contact us so we can take appropriate action.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-50 mb-2">Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>We may update this policy occasionally. Changes will be posted on this page with an updated effective date.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-50 mb-2">Contact</h2>
          <p>This site is operated by <strong class="text-surface-50">Pushkar Saini</strong>, StudyRoadmap, Delhi, India. If you have questions about this privacy policy or a data request, reach out using the same email you will see on the contact page:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 mt-2">
            <li>
              <a href="mailto:pushkersaini@gmail.com" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline dark:text-brand-400">
                pushkersaini@gmail.com
              </a>
              — privacy questions and data requests
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/author/pushkar-saini/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline dark:text-brand-400">
                Editor profile
              </a>
              — named operator
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="/feedback/" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline dark:text-brand-400">
                Submit feedback
              </a>
              — for bug reports and feature suggestions
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
